l}, {"t_ms": 56560, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014LBQHTA6BQ8DbrpY8eWbds", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 56560, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014LBQHTA6BQ8DbrpY8eWbds", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 58905, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01DvWVcfB5moXW9oMDGHHb3N", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 59205, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01DvWVcfB5moXW9oMDGHHb3N", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 59205, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DvWVcfB5moXW9oMDGHHb3N", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 64394, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **What was broken:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with about 18% of requests erroring. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy.\n- **Which version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **First attempt failed partway:** the deployment tool hit an error and stopped after us-east. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while the other two regions stayed on v2.3.1. I retried once and it went through everywhere.\n- **Now:** all regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created. I didn't retry, so the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- The incident describes what failed, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed before deploying it again.\n  - Look into the deployment tool error that stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01BYtt2TS3W1og5QSNmYSxaw", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_012BooTQ3o6ywmeCfbdAXLFt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01D3RABBznPzq8gULGFxFKUf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01NVSzXJEENRi5WxVyFZqhCt", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Only us-east got rolled back. I'll retry the rollback once, since it targets the same known-healthy version.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01GdKu4QZSX2Vx3vFWGszLiA", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01AqoJAjFEjHatxRH93Fk7Ke", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01NmkLbi9dxNzMQzSezR6KSd", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014LBQHTA6BQ8DbrpY8eWbds", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. Deployment history: v2.2.9 healthy, v2.3.0 healthy, v2.3.1-rc unhealthy, v2.3.1 unhealthy. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release. The first rollback attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, which left the service on mixed versions (us-east v2.3.0, us-west/eu-west v2.3.1). A retry completed successfully. Current state: all regions on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Follow-ups: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 (and v2.3.1-rc) failures before redeploying, and investigate the orchestrator error that halted the first rollback."}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "The request timed out, so the incident may or may not exist. I'll check before retrying so the on-call engineer doesn't get paged twice.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01DvWVcfB5moXW9oMDGHHb3N", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and the service is healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**.\n\n**Rollback**\n- **What was broken:** v2.3.1 was running in us-east, us-west and eu-west and failing health checks, with about 18% of requests erroring. Its release candidate (v2.3.1-rc) had also been unhealthy.\n- **Which version:** v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so it didn't need change-manager approval.\n- **First attempt failed partway:** the deployment tool hit an error and stopped after us-east. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while the other two regions stayed on v2.3.1. I retried once and it went through everywhere.\n- **Now:** all regions are on v2.3.0, health checks pass, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n\n**Incident**\n- The request to create the incident timed out, but when I checked the incident list it had been created. I didn't retry, so the on-call engineer was paged once.\n- The incident describes what failed, the rollback (including the partial failure and retry) and two follow-ups:\n  - Find out why v2.3.1 failed before deploying it again.\n  - Look into the deployment tool error that stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}